   "id": "bd1baf84-0715-48c0-bacf-cb5719e0f48d",
   "term": "Microphone output transformer",
   "verdict": "MINOR",
   "suggestions": [
    {
     "field": "definition",
     "severity": "Low",
     "issue": "Definition says the transformer 'impedance-matches the capsule output to the microphone cable and connected preamp,' but the sibling entry Mic Output Impedance explicitly teaches that mic-to-preamp connection is bridging, NOT impedance matching, and lists 'thinking you should impedance-match the mic to the preamp' as a common mistake. A learner meeting both entries gets contradictory language about 'matching' vs 'bridging.'",
     "suggestion": "Reword to avoid the mic-to-preamp 'matching' framing, e.g. 'transforms the high impedance of the capsule/electronics down to a low, balanced output impedance suited to the cable and to a bridging (higher-impedance) preamp input,' so it aligns with the bridging concept taught elsewhere in the glossary."
    }
   ]
